  <url><loc>https://dagric.com/features</loc><lastmod>2026-08-03</lastmod><priority>0.8</priority></url>
  <!-- The guide is generated into site/guide/ by tools/publish-guide.py, which is
       why it was the one page set missing here: it is not hand-written next to the
       others. It is still the highest-intent content on the site — 21 sections
       answering "will my printer work" for someone deciding whether to leave
       Windows.

       DO NOT EDIT BETWEEN THE MARKERS. This block is regenerated by
       publish-guide.py from its PAGES dict, and hand edits are overwritten on the
       next run. It used to be hand-written, under a comment asking whoever adds a
       language to add its URL here in the same commit — and that instruction
       survived exactly one language. Four translations shipped and this file still
       listed two, so /guide/es, /fr, /it and /pt-br existed, cross-linked and
       carried hreflang, and nothing told a crawler they were there. To add a
       language, add it to PAGES and run the script. -->
